<p><span>Cold sores can be painful and leave you feeling stressed and self-conscious.</span></p>
<p><span>Whether you’re experiencing an outbreak or are looking for daily suppression management, our cold core treatment options are here to help.</span></p>

<p><span>Cold sores, also known as ‘fever blisters’, are a common viral infection that is most commonly caused by the herpes simplex virus type 1 (HSV-1). The virus is transmitted by close contact with an infected person, usually through broken skin, and generally through sexual activity.</span></p>
<p><span>There is currently no cure for core sores and outbreaks can be frequent, causing sores and blisters around the mouth and facial areas. However, symptoms can be easily managed with antiviral medications and topical creams.</span></p>
<p><b>Our Partner Doctors can assist you with the medication you need to manage symptoms of an outbreak or prescribe you with up to 3 months of preventive treatment, which can suppress the virus and reduce cold sore outbreaks by up to 80% with the use of daily medication.</b></p>
